---
/* The background of every public page (owner request, 25 October 2026: "improve the backgrounds, try something new …
   glassmorphism with AI reference grid … not boring"). One fixed layer behind the content, so sections glide over it as
   the page scrolls, with no animation: a fine reference grid of dots that fades toward the middle of the screen, and two
   soft brand glows. (The North Star, the owner's word for his direction, is the mark in the bar of websites,
   site-switch.astro, where nothing scrolls under it.) Sections and cards over it are glass
   (translucent token surfaces, site.css), not blurred, so scrolling stays smooth. Decorative: aria-hidden. Hidden when
   the visitor asks for less transparency, in forced colours, and in print. */
---
<div class="ai-field" aria-hidden="true"></div>

<style>
  .ai-field { position: fixed; inset: 0; z-index: -1; pointer-events: none; overflow: hidden; background: var(--glow-cyan) no-repeat right -18vw top -22vh / min(72vw, 860px) min(72vw, 860px), var(--glow-blue) no-repeat left -18vw bottom -26vh / min(80vw, 940px) min(80vw, 940px); }
  :global([dir="rtl"]) .ai-field { background-position: left -18vw top -22vh, right -18vw bottom -26vh; }
  /* A glass veil over the glows: text can sit on a glow's peak as the page scrolls, and the veil keeps every text colour
     at 4.5:1 or more there (measured at the peak: links 4.63 in light, 5.29 in dark; without it 3.50 and 3.66). The veil
     is whole over the content column and thins only in the margins beside it, where no text sits, so on a wide screen
     the glows show at their strength there (a laptop's margins are narrower than the fade, so the veil stays whole). */
  .ai-field::after { --field-edge: max(0px, calc((100vw - var(--container-max)) / 2)); content: ""; position: absolute; inset: 0; background: var(--surface-glass); -webkit-mask-image: linear-gradient(90deg, rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.3) 0, #000 var(--field-edge), #000 calc(100% - var(--field-edge)), rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.3) 100%); mask-image: linear-gradient(90deg, rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.3) 0, #000 var(--field-edge), #000 calc(100% - var(--field-edge)), rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.3) 100%); }
  /* The reference grid, above the veil: a brand-tinted dot every 28px and a faint major line every five dots, like graph
     paper; strongest at the edges of the screen, gone in the middle where text is read. */
  .ai-field::before { content: ""; position: absolute; inset: 0; z-index: 1; background-image: radial-gradient(circle, var(--field-dot) 1.2px, transparent 1.8px), linear-gradient(var(--field-line) 1px, transparent 1px), linear-gradient(90deg, var(--field-line) 1px, transparent 1px); background-size: 28px 28px, 140px 140px, 140px 140px; background-position: 0 0, -14px -14px, -14px -14px; -webkit-mask-image: radial-gradient(ellipse 70% 65% at 50% 45%, transparent 35%, #000 100%); mask-image: radial-gradient(ellipse 70% 65% at 50% 45%, transparent 35%, #000 100%); }
  @media (prefers-reduced-transparency: reduce) { .ai-field { display: none; } }
  @media (forced-colors: active) { .ai-field { display: none; } }
  @media print { .ai-field { display: none; } }
</style>
